  "timing_acceptance": false,
  "problem": "C64 scoped helpers skipped occupied keys, but a required consumer picking an optional queued key could still block on a second owner even after its originally required value completed.",
  "implementation": "Both optional helper origins now share the nonblocking queued-key path, selected with an explicit Waiting/Scoped origin and separate actual ready/busy/owned counters. A busy waiter-picked key returns to the original required cell loop. Required direct consumers and all prerequisites inside a newly owned initializer keep get_or_init. Cell ownership/publication/panic handling, pending mutex/recheck/Condvar protocol, queue bounds, TLS ancestor guard, scoped joining and source-ordered writer consumption are unchanged by this refinement. C62-C64 production foundations remain held; accepted C60 is the baseline.",
