  "design_review": {
    "status": "source review; validation in progress",
    "source_revision": "4f3328815786a38164f1ccc400893a1eba985549",
    "native_tree": "8be33d42e43dbaa3278c9d1f7072c96f2fc13e74",
    "accepted_baseline": "60e210d1b0e459955aec2007d8231ee4358bed88",
    "scope": "Held C62-C64 queue/scoped foundation plus nonblocking optional waiter-picked claims. Existing held variants remain diagnostic controls, not accepted baselines.",
    "invariants": [
      "Every original direct anchor/column consumer stays required; only the key selected from the help queue is optional. A newly owned anchor still evaluates all mandatory dependencies through get_or_init.",
      "No Cell implementation, pending mutex, lost-wakeup protocol, queue capacity, helper permit, TLS ancestor guard or writer ordering is changed by this refinement.",
      "Both helper origins share try_anchor. An explicit enum selects attempted/ready/busy/owned counters once per queued call. Recursive direct calls never inherit that origin.",
      "Existing dependency_helped_anchors counts waiter-picked attempts; ready/owned include cached/new failures, Busy skips another owner. Lookup failure is an attempt without a claim class. Errors retain their exact text through Planner.fail.",
      "Busy returns to the original get_or_init loop, which rechecks its own value and ownership under the original synchronization protocol before selecting more work or sleeping.",
      "Scopes still join before root check, publication and cleanup; no new per-cell or per-job storage except three optional metric counters."
    ],
    "tests_added": [
      "Required waiter on A skips busy B, initializes C which releases A, and returns before B is released. Both controlled owners are released on observation timeout; correct original result, exact queue order, one C initializer and eventual B result are checked."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "Quiet timing confirmation is deferred and unrelated host load must be retained in evidence.",
      "Nonblocking optional helpers can pick/reoffer the same still-owned descriptor through different consumers. Inspect offered/attempt/owned counts for queue churn before assuming fewer waits means less work.",
      "Low ownership counts do not establish useful CPU time or wall-time shares. Required dependency waits and shared broadcasts still exist."
    ]
  },
