  "counter_definition": "Counts cover profile lifetime including1warmup+1measured region. Each queued call gets its own origin; recursive direct calls do not inherit it. Ready/owned include cached/new errors; Busy means a skipped occupied claim. Attempts include pre-claim lookup failures. Existing helped_anchors is waiter attempts; drained counts only successful scoped ready/owned resolutions. Offered descriptors may repeat a key after removal and are not unique-cell counts. Optional ownership is not a time share. Join-nanosecond counters include nested helping and overlap; they are not idle or elapsed-time shares.",
  "memory": "ColumnCell stays32bytes versus accepted C60\u2019s 24. This refinement adds no cell storage or ownership; three opt-in counters are added. All scoped tasks and planner borrows still join before publication/cleanup. Process peak RSS includes startup/warmup and is not a sustained-memory bound.",
  "observer_definition": "Task spans include waits and preemption; process CPU includes service/shader/observer work. Target/helper counts and long tasks remain separate, and physical-thread unions count one thread once. Helper success includes skipped Busy calls. Tail runs through the last target/helper finish after p95 target completion. Separate diagnostic runs under changed host load are not causal speedup comparisons.",
  "decision": "Held, unmerged. Main Nether, custom bounds and direct stem lose aggregate throughput. The second seed has only a small aggregate improvement, and both standard-seed p95s worsen. Overworld is also slightly lower in throughput, with a worse p95. Known host load precludes quiet acceptance, and these observations do not select this scheduler. Main remains C60; the subsecond/concurrency/lifecycle/memory goal is still open.",
  "next_experiment": "Return to accepted origin/main without C62-C65 production scheduling changes. Extend the test-only worker-phase observer to record noninitializer dependency-cell join intervals, then intersect them with per-worker task and tail spans. Preserve reentrant task contexts, missing/failure data and joined buffer cleanup; do not call API join intervals kernel-sleep or CPU time. Measure the remaining tail before adding further scheduler complexity. See external cycle65/conditional-next-measurement.md.",
  "limitations": [
    "Quiet final timing confirmation remains deferred; host observations are retained.",
    "No reverse/concurrent/portal/retention acceptance was added for this unselected candidate.",
    "The full subsecond median/p95, no-regression, concurrency/lifecycle and sustained-memory requirements remain open."
